== seed doc proj/geo
package geo // import "geo"

Package geo has shapes and their measurements, for the tests of seed
doc.

Areas are in square meters:

  geo.area(geo.Shape.Square(2.0)) is 4.0

CONSTANTS

const int triangleSides = 3
const int squareSides = 4
    The sides of the shapes, as `Shape` counts them.

FUNCTIONS

fn area(Shape s) float
    The area of s.

fn undocumented() int

fn named(string name) Named
    A named shape with no outline.

TYPES

type Shape enum {
    // A circle of the radius.
    Circle(float radius)
    Square(float side)
    // Nothing at all.
    Empty
}
    A shape. Use `area` for its area and `units.Meter` for lengths.

type Named struct {
    string name = "unnamed"
    // The outline, in meters.
    units.Meter outline
    // Has fields that are not pub.
}
    A shape with its name and the length of its outline.

fn (Named n) label() string
    The name, or "unnamed".

type Measured interface {
    // The area, in square meters.
    area() float
    mut scale(float by)
}
    Something with an area.

-- exit 0
